tinylinalg is an independently written MIT implementation of standard vector,
matrix, partial-pivoting LU, Cholesky, and cyclic Jacobi algorithms.
No NumPy, SciPy, LAPACK, or Vallado source is included in the runtime.
The test fixtures contain numerical outputs obtained from NumPy 2.5.4 and
SciPy 1.18.1. Their original software is used only during development.
